!
! VMS$VMS.DAT - STDRV component registration database
!
! OVMX-DEFINED FORMAT (CLAUDE.md Rule 8): only the FILE NAME is observed
! from the OpenVMS Alpha V8.4 oracle (docs/design-boot-faithful.md sec 3.3,
! DIRECTORY SYS$STARTUP:*.DAT). VSI's internal byte layout for this file was
! never read and is not reproduced here -- this line format is an OVMX
! invention, parsed by SYS$MANAGER:STARTUP.COM's RUN_COMPONENTS subroutine.
!
! One component per line:
!
!     phase-name  procedure-filespec
!
! separated by whitespace. "phase-name" must exactly match one of the nine
! names in SYS$STARTUP:VMS$PHASES.DAT. STARTUP.COM runs "procedure-filespec"
! (with @) when its phase comes up in the driver loop. Lines beginning with
! "!" and blank lines are comments/ignored.
!
! SCS (vms-5ad, child of vms-110b) is registered at CONFIG, the fourth of
! the nine phases -- after DEVICES (so the executive's device table has
! already surfaced ETH0:, the NIC SCSD self-resolves and binds -- see
! SYS$STARTUP:SCS_STARTUP.COM's own header) and well before the
! layered-product/site phases (LPBEGIN/LPMAIN/LPBETA). SCS/cluster
! connection management is core infrastructure, not a layered product or a
! site choice, so it belongs early -- the same reasoning JOB_CONTROL's
! header below gives for CONFIG being tried first there. UNLIKE
! JOB_CONTROL, that early placement is NOT reverted here: JOB_CONTROL had
! to move to END because its child LOGINOUT session prompts on the shared
! OPA0: console AND KEEPS the console (an interactive login loop) while
! STARTUP.COM is still writing to it (see below). SCSD is different: it is a
! detached daemon that writes only a couple of SCSD-I-* startup lines to
! OPA0: (cluster state is OPCOM/operator-console traffic on real VMS) and
! then goes quiet on the wire -- the brief interleave with STARTUP.COM's
! CONFIG-phase output is the same interleave real VMS cluster startup has,
! an accepted reality rather than the persistent garble a login loop causes,
! so CONFIG is safe. (SCSD cannot log to a file instead: a detached
! process's $CREPRC /OUTPUT is a raw open() that cannot create a file on the
! ACP-served ODS-2 system disk -- tracked as a vms-7eb follow-up.)
!
! JOB_CONTROL (vms-2a9, docs/design-boot-faithful.md sec3.8/sec4.5) is
! OVMX's first real component registration: SYS$STARTUP:JOB_CONTROL_
! STARTUP.COM, which RUN/DETACHED's JOB_CONTROL.EXE, the process that owns
! the console login loop (vms-8d2). It runs at END, the LAST of the nine
! phases -- an OVMX DESIGN CHOICE (Rule 8), not an oracle capture, and NOT
! the choice this project started with. VSI never publishes which phase
! internally starts the job controller, so CONFIG (an early phase, on the
! reasoning that JOB_CONTROL is a core OS service rather than a layered
! product or a site choice) was tried FIRST. MEASURED, against a real QEMU
! boot (tests/qemu/test_boot_conformance.sh): starting JOB_CONTROL that
! early creates a real defect, not just a documentation mismatch -- its
! child LOGINOUT session begins prompting "Username:" on the shared
! console WHILE STARTUP.COM's own phase driver is still writing to that
! same console (SYCONFIG.COM, SYLOGICALS.COM, SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM's
! INSTALL ADD lines and site announcement), and the two interleave into
! garbled output. END avoids this by construction: STARTUP.COM's OWN last
! console output finishes at LPMAIN (SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM's trailing WRITE)
! before RUN_PHASES even reaches LPBETA/END, so JOB_CONTROL is created
! only after nothing else will ever write to the console again -- the
! EXACT ordering this project's boot already had, and had already tested
! clean, before this item existed (JOB_CONTROL was the last call inside
! SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM, itself the last real action of the LPMAIN phase).
! This item's job was to make that ordering REACHED THROUGH the
! declarative component mechanism instead of a hardcoded call, not to
! change when JOB_CONTROL starts -- END is what "unchanged" means once
! independently expressed as a registration.
!
! Before this item JOB_CONTROL was created by a hardcoded `@SYS$STARTUP:
! JOB_CONTROL_STARTUP.COM` line inside SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (the
! LPMAIN site file) -- functionally identical to the line below, but
! invisible to the phase-driven mechanism this file exists to drive;
! removing the line below (and nothing else) now stops JOB_CONTROL from
! ever being created (tests/qemu/test_job_control_negctl.sh proves exactly
! that against a real boot).
!
CONFIG SYS$STARTUP:SCS_STARTUP.COM
END SYS$STARTUP:JOB_CONTROL_STARTUP.COM
